==Trivia==
* In [[Chuang Yi]]'s English translation of the {{ma|Jirachi: Wish Maker|manga adaptation}} of ''Jirachi: Wish Maker'', Forina is spelled as "Ferina".

===Origin===
{{main|Pokémon world in relation to the real world#In the movies|Pokémon world in relation to the real world → In the movies}}
Forina is based on {{wp|Wulingyuan}}, a scenic area and a UNESCO World Heritage Site located in the province of {{wp|Hunan}} in {{wp|China}}. The site is dominated by thousands of {{wp|quartzite}} {{wp|sandstone}} pillars several hundred meters high that are spread across the forested landscape.

The production notes in the official Japanese movie pamphlet reveals that Director [[Kunihiko Yuyama|Yuyama]] found his inspiration for the setting after seeing a photo of Wulingyuan on a magazine cover. He noted that the tall rock formations would provide a sense of scale for the aerial battle, along with the mysterious atmosphere surrounding the site would make it an ideal spot for Jirachi to hibernate.

